  ],
  "slug": "ai-topic-c4ec",
  "summary": "Three preprints add structured priors and denoised representations for unseen-perturbation response prediction, while two published papers extend knowledge-guided property prediction.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is predicting transcriptional responses to unseen genetic perturbations by injecting structure beyond expression data. Graph-guided Flow Matching couples knowledge graphs with latent flow matching for unseen Perturb-seq targets. OCCAM uses an MLP over denoised single-cell representations combined with gene interaction, text and protein features. S1Pert predicts target-specific responses using Welch/equivalence-testing labels and a frozen encoder. The common move is replacing end-to-end expression modeling with external biological priors or curated representations. Two published items, ReMoD-Mol (multimodal fusion with descriptor-guided distillation) and ontology pre-training for metabolites, are adjacent: they apply knowledge-informed learning to molecular property prediction rather than cellular perturbation response.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-18"
}
